From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a folder a user makes in a setgid tree keeps the bit

In a system prefix ProgramData is sgsystem:sgwine 2775 with an inheriting default ACL. The client's fchmod of a folder it had just made applied the server's mode, which has no setgid, and took the bit off: the next folder down got its maker's own group, and SYSTEM could not replace what a user had made there (Epic's elevated launcher: EC-PRM). The bit mkdir gave is kept.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 0076064..299eb26 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -4725,6 +4725,18 @@ NTSTATUS open_unix_file( HANDLE *handle, const char *unix_name, ACCESS_MASK acce
          * Program Files' "others r-x" made every installed program every
          * account's to change */
         else m &= 07000 | limit;
+#endif
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SETGID_DROPPED
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a folder made in a setgid one (ProgramData's
+         * tree: the users' group, sgwine) got the bit from mkdir, and this
+         * fchmod with the server's mode took it off: what was made in it
+         * next got its maker's own group, and SYSTEM (sgsystem, in sgwine)
+         * could not write it -- Epic's launcher, its update data made by a
+         * user and replaced by its elevated copy, failed (EC-PRM) */
+        {
+            struct stat dir_st;
+            if (!fstat( fd, &dir_st ) && S_ISDIR( dir_st.st_mode ) && (dir_st.st_mode & S_ISGID)) m |= S_ISGID;
+        }
 #endif
         fchmod( fd, m );
     }
